# ---- SWAGAT-FI ----
add("SWG/EFF/801","SW",2,"Applied in May, tagged when?",
 [["Applicant","Regulated pension fund"],["Applied","20 May 2026"],["Request","Tag as SWAGAT-FI immediately"],["Circular","Dated 16 January 2026"]],
 "When can the tag take effect?",
 ["16 January 2026","From 1 June 2026, when the circular comes into force","1 April 2027","Immediately on application"],1,
 "The SWAGAT-FI circular is dated 16 January 2026 but its provisions came into force on 1 June 2026.",
 ["The circular date isn't its effective date.",None,"1 April 2027 isn't the effective date.","The tag follows the circular's effective date."],
 "SEBI circular 16 Jan 2026, para 5")
add("SWG/APP/802","SW",1,"How to apply for SWAGAT",
 [["FPI","Existing Category I mutual fund"],["Wants","SWAGAT-FI status"],["Question","What does it submit to the DDP?"],["Evidence","Prospectus extracts ready"]],
 "What starts the process?",
 ["A fresh FPI application form","The SWAGAT requisition letter (Annex A) with supporting documents","An email to SEBI","Nothing; DDPs tag eligible FPIs automatically"],1,
 "For registration or reclassification as SWAGAT-FI, the applicant gives its DDP the SWAGAT requisition letter in the Annex A format, with supporting documents or web links.",
 ["Existing FPIs don't need a fresh application.",None,"The request goes to the DDP, not SEBI.","The FPI must opt in; it isn't automatic."],
 "SWAGAT SOP 27 May 2026, section 3 A.1–A.2; Annex A")
add("SWG/TAG/803","SW",1,"How SWAGAT status shows up",
 [["DDP","Approves a SWAGAT-FI application"],["Question","Where is the status recorded?"],["Registrations","FPI and FVCI"],["System","FPI registration portal and depository"]],
 "How is it recorded?",
 ["A note in the DDP's internal file only","SWAGAT-FI-FPI and SWAGAT-FI-FVCI flags on the portal and the depository","A new registration number","A separate certificate from SEBI"],1,
 "The depository provides for selecting the SWAGAT-FI-FPI and SWAGAT-FI-FVCI flags on the FPI registration portal and in the depository system.",
 ["The status is flagged in shared systems, not just internally.",None,"The registration number doesn't change.","SEBI doesn't issue a separate certificate."],
 "SWAGAT SOP 27 May 2026, section 3 B.3")
add("SWG/UNI/804","SW",2,"One view of FPI and FVCI holdings",
 [["Investor","SWAGAT-FI holding listed equity as an FPI and startup shares as an FVCI"],["Question","How do the depositories show its holdings?"],["Wish","One consolidated view"],["Status","SWAGAT-FI tagged"]],
 "What do depositories provide?",
 ["Separate, unconnected accounts","A single unified account and investing experience","A view only for FPI holdings","Nothing; it must reconcile itself"],1,
 "Depositories facilitate a single unified accounting and investing experience for SWAGAT-FIs, so securities held as an FPI, an FVCI, or a foreign investor in investment vehicles are kept in a unified manner.",
 ["The circular requires a unified experience.",None,"FVCI holdings are included.","Depositories have a duty to facilitate this."],
 "SEBI circular 16 Jan 2026, para 3.2 (vi)(IV)")
add("SWG/INS/805","SW",3,"Government-owned reinsurer",
 [["FPI","Reinsurer 100% owned by a foreign government"],["Registered as","Appropriately regulated insurance company"],["Portfolio","Includes some segregated accounts"],["Request","SWAGAT-FI"]],
 "Under which route can it qualify?",
 ["None; segregated accounts disqualify it","As a government-related investor","Only as a pension fund","As an insurer, ignoring the segregated accounts"],1,
 "The SOP says an insurer or reinsurer eligible for registration as a government-related investor, but registered under the insurance sub-category, is eligible for SWAGAT-FI as a government-related investor. That route has no segregated-portfolio test.",
 ["The government-related route remains open.",None,"It isn't a pension fund.","The insurance route does have the segregated-portfolio test."],
 "SWAGAT SOP 27 May 2026, section 8, row 3 note")
add("SWG/PEN/806","SW",3,"Pension fund that also fits the mutual fund route",
 [["FPI","Registered under the pension-fund sub-category"],["Also qualifies as","Appropriately regulated retail unit trust"],["Question","Which SWAGAT route can it use?"],["Evidence","Available for both"]],
 "What are its options?",
 ["Only the pension-fund route","Government-related or retail fund status, as applicable","None; it must re-register first","Whichever has the lower fee"],1,
 "The SOP lets entities registered as pension funds that are also eligible as a mutual fund or government-related investor seek SWAGAT-FI status under those classifications, as applicable.",
 ["The SOP allows the other routes too.",None,"No re-registration is needed.","Fees don't decide the route."],
 "SWAGAT SOP 27 May 2026, section 8, row 4")
add("SWG/PEN/807","SW",3,"Evidence for a US pension plan",
 [["Applicant","US corporate pension plan"],["Route","SWAGAT-FI as pension fund"],["Question","What evidence does the SOP point to?"],["Regulators","Department of Labor; IRS"]],
 "Which evidence fits?",
 ["A letter from its bank","A Department of Labor (Form 5500) record or a certified IRS determination letter","An SEC fund registration","A self-declaration"],1,
 "The SOP's Annex C lists the US Department of Labor (ERISA, with a Form 5500 search) or the Internal Revenue Service, where a certified copy of the determination letter is proof of tax-exempt pension status.",
 ["A bank letter isn't the listed evidence.",None,"SEC registration is for funds, not pension plans.","A self-declaration isn't enough."],
 "SWAGAT SOP 27 May 2026, Annex C (United States)")
add("SWG/SGP/808","SW",3,"Checking a Singapore fund",
 [["Applicant","Singapore collective investment scheme"],["DDP task","Confirm it's a public retail fund"],["Tool","MAS OPERA portal"],["Question","Where to look?"]],
 "What does the SOP say to check?",
 ["MAS's list of licensed banks","OPERA's 'Offers for CIS' section: authorised schemes (Singapore) or recognised schemes (foreign)","The Singapore company registry","The fund's website"],1,
 "OPERA holds offer documents lodged with MAS. Under 'Offers for CIS', schemes constituted in Singapore are Authorised Schemes and those constituted abroad are Recognised Schemes.",
 ["The bank list doesn't show fund status.",None,"The company registry doesn't show retail-fund status.","The SOP points to the regulator's portal."],
 "SWAGAT SOP 27 May 2026, Annex B (Singapore)")
add("SWG/CAN/809","SW",3,"Canadian mutual fund's retail status",
 [["Applicant","Canadian mutual fund"],["Regulation","National Instrument 81-102"],["Gap","The rules don't require every mutual fund to be open to retail"],["Question","How does the DDP confirm retail access?"]],
 "What does the SOP suggest?",
 ["Assume retail, since it's a mutual fund","Check SEDAR+ and confirm retail access from the simplified prospectus","Ask the Ontario Securities Commission for a letter","Retail status can't be confirmed for Canadian funds"],1,
 "The SOP notes that NI 81-101 doesn't mandate retail access, so the prospectus is used. Funds recognised as a conventional or alternative mutual fund on SEDAR+ that file a simplified prospectus can be treated as public retail funds after checking it.",
 ["The SOP marks retail access To Be Verified.",None,"A regulator letter isn't the suggested route.","It can be confirmed from the prospectus."],
 "SWAGAT SOP 27 May 2026, Annex B (Canada)")
add("SWG/MAL/810","SW",3,"Malaysian unit trust",
 [["Applicant","Malaysian unit trust fund"],["Regulator","Securities Commission Malaysia"],["Gap","Guidelines don't require unit trusts to be open to retail"],["Question","What evidence settles retail access?"]],
 "What does the SOP say?",
 ["Nothing needed; unit trusts are retail by law","Check the prospectus or trust deed for subscription restrictions","Malaysian funds can't qualify","A board resolution from the manager"],1,
 "The SOP notes that Malaysia's Guidelines on Unit Trust Funds don't mandate retail access, so the prospectus or trust deed is used to check for subscription restrictions.",
 ["The SOP marks retail access To Be Verified.",None,"Malaysian unit trusts are listed in Annex B.","A board resolution isn't the suggested evidence."],
 "SWAGAT SOP 27 May 2026, Annex B (Malaysia)")
add("SWG/IFS/811","SW",2,"GIFT City retail scheme",
 [["Applicant","Retail scheme in GIFT IFSC"],["Regulator","IFSCA, under the Fund Management Regulations 2025"],["Manager","IFSCA-registered fund management entity"],["Question","Can it be a public retail fund for SWAGAT?"]],
 "Does it qualify?",
 ["No. Only foreign jurisdictions are identified","Yes. IFSCA retail schemes are listed as meeting the public retail fund conditions","Only if it also registers in Luxembourg","Only as Category II"],1,
 "The SOP's Annex B lists retail schemes under the IFSCA Fund Management Regulations 2025 as meeting all five public retail fund conditions.",
 ["GIFT IFSC is specifically listed.",None,"No foreign registration is needed.","Category doesn't decide SWAGAT eligibility."],
 "SWAGAT SOP 27 May 2026, Annex B (GIFT IFSC)")
add("SWG/HK/812","SW",2,"Hong Kong MPF scheme",
 [["Applicant","Mandatory Provident Fund scheme"],["Registered with","Hong Kong MPF Schemes Authority"],["Route sought","SWAGAT-FI as a pension fund"],["Question","Recognised in the SOP?"]],
 "Can it use the pension route?",
 ["No. Hong Kong isn't covered","Yes. MPF and ORSO schemes registered with the MPFA are listed","Only as a retail unit trust","Only if government owned"],1,
 "Annex C lists Hong Kong's Mandatory Provident Fund Schemes Authority. MPF schemes registered under the MPF Schemes Ordinance and occupational schemes registered under ORSO are retirement schemes for this purpose.",
 ["Hong Kong appears in Annex C.",None,"The pension route is available.","Government ownership isn't required for pension funds."],
 "SWAGAT SOP 27 May 2026, Annex C (Hong Kong)")
add("SWG/REN/813","SW",1,"Renewing a SWAGAT-FI FPI",
 [["FPI","SWAGAT-FI, FPI registration only"],["Event","First 10-year block ending"],["Question","What does renewal involve?"],["Changes","One change in directors"]],
 "What's required?",
 ["A full new application","Pay the US$2,500 renewal fee and inform any changes","Nothing; status is permanent","Pay US$250 and a no-change declaration"],1,
 "A SWAGAT-FI continuing for the next 10-year block pays the renewal fee to its DDP (US$2,500 for FPI only) and informs any changes in information submitted earlier.",
 ["Renewal isn't a new application.",None,"Renewal is still due every 10 years.","US$250 is the regular Category II fee."],
 "SWAGAT SOP 27 May 2026, section 3 B.4–B.5; circular 16 Jan 2026, para 3.3")
add("SWG/CTL/814","SW",2,"One investor steers the fund",
 [["Applicant","Regulated unit trust, open to retail"],["Investor base","One institution holds 60% and directs investment choices"],["Manager","Follows that investor's instructions"],["Request","SWAGAT-FI"]],
 "Does it meet the retail fund conditions?",
 ["Yes. It's regulated and open to retail","No. Contributors mustn't control operations, and the manager must be independent of them","Yes, if the investor drops below 50%","Only as a pension fund"],1,
 "A public retail fund must operate as a blind pool with diversified investors, contributors must not control day-to-day operations, and the manager must be independent of contributors. A dominant investor directing the manager fails these tests.",
 ["Being open to retail is only one of five conditions.",None,"The test is control and independence, not a 50% line.","It isn't a pension fund."],
 "SEBI circular 16 Jan 2026, para 3.2 (vi)(I)(b)")
